findings.description:
FIND — `_compute_rho` does not validate that `novelty_counts` and `raw_counts` have the same length. The rolling window loop indexes both arrays with the same `i`:
for i in range(max(0, len(raw_counts) - cfg.rho_rolling_window), len(raw_counts)):
    if raw_counts[i] > 0:
        rho_values.append(novelty_counts[i] / raw_counts[i])
If `len(novelty_counts) < len(raw_counts)`, this raises `IndexError`. The function signature accepts them independently with no length assertion.
